  "contract": {
    "operation": "Iteratively trim zero-in-degree or zero-out-degree active vertices as singleton SCCs, choose the lowest-ID pivot in each remaining subgraph, intersect its forward and backward reachable sets, and recurse on forward-only, backward-only, and neither-reachable vertex sets.",
    "pivot_rule": "Lowest vertex ID in each active subgraph.",
    "trim_rule": "Each trim pass removes every currently active vertex with no active incoming or no active outgoing arc; repeat until no more vertices are trim candidates.",
    "profile_projection": "The source's CUDA pivot hash and parallel scheduling are replaced by a deterministic smallest-ID pivot and canonical minimum-vertex labels. The FB reachability, subgraph partition, and repeated trivial-SCC trimming operations are retained.",
